+    <section class="slide feature" data-title="The Method Atlas" aria-labelledby="s2-title"><div class="slide-inner"><div class="feature-copy"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Orientation</p><h2 class="title" id="s2-title">The method atlas</h2><ul class="method-list"><li><b>JP</b><span>Grill · simmer · stuff & braise</span><span>3 dishes</span></li><li><b>KR</b><span>Stir-fry · blanch & toss · griddle-fry</span><span>3 dishes</span></li><li><b>CN</b><span>Deep-fry · steam</span><span>2 dishes</span></li><li><b>TW</b><span>Reduce · soup</span><span>2 dishes</span></li></ul></div><figure class="feature-media"><img src="assets/generated/atlas/generate-media-replicate_z_image_turbo-1.png" alt="Fresh squid displayed on ice at a coastal fish market"><figcaption>Ten methods · four traditions</figcaption></figure></div></section>
+    <section class="slide feature" data-title="Prep the Squid" aria-labelledby="s3-title"><div class="slide-inner"><div class="feature-copy"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Knife work</p><h2 class="title" id="s3-title">Prep the squid</h2><div class="prep-grid"><div><strong>Pull</strong><p>Separate head and innards from the mantle in one steady motion.</p></div><div><strong>Trim</strong><p>Cut below the eyes; keep tentacles, discard beak and innards.</p></div><div><strong>Clean</strong><p>Remove quill and rinse the cavity. Peel skin only for a pale finish.</p></div><div><strong>Dry</strong><p>Blot thoroughly. Surface water defeats browning and crisp coatings.</p></div></div></div><figure class="feature-media"><img src="assets/generated/prep/generate-media-replicate_z_image_turbo-1.png" alt="Cleaned squid parts arranged on a cutting board"><figcaption>One mantle · two fins · tentacles</figcaption></figure></div></section>
+    <section class="slide feature" data-title="Heat Is the Choice" aria-labelledby="s4-title"><div class="slide-inner"><div class="feature-copy"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Texture logic</p><h2 class="title" id="s4-title">Heat is the choice</h2><p class="dek">Squid is tender at the edges of time: cook it very fast, or let it relax slowly.</p><ul class="method-list"><li><b>0–2 min</b><span>Flash cook</span><span>tender snap</span></li><li><b>3–15 min</b><span>Avoid the middle</span><span>rubbery</span></li><li><b>25–60 min</b><span>Gentle braise</span><span>silky again</span></li></ul></div><figure class="feature-media"><img src="assets/generated/heat/generate-media-replicate_z_image_turbo-1.png" alt="Scored squid cooking quickly in a hot wok"><figcaption>High heat · short contact</figcaption></figure></div></section>
