+    <section class="slide recipe" data-title="Ikayaki" aria-labelledby="s5-title"><div class="slide-inner"><figure class="recipe-photo"><img src="assets/generated/ikayaki/generate-media-replicate_z_image_turbo-1.png" alt="Japanese soy-glazed grilled squid"><figcaption>Method 01 · grill</figcaption></figure><article class="recipe-content"><header class="recipe-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Japan · festival & izakaya tradition</p><h2 class="title" id="s5-title">Ikayaki</h2><p class="tradition">Soy-glazed grilled whole squid</p></div><div class="timebox"><strong>20</strong><span>10 prep · 10 cook</span></div></header><div class="recipe-body"><section><h3 class="label">Ingredients · serves 4</h3><ul class="ingredients"><li><b>500 g</b> cleaned whole squid</li><li><b>2 tbsp</b> soy sauce</li><li><b>2 tbsp</b> mirin</li><li><b>1 tbsp</b> sake</li><li><b>2 tsp</b> grated ginger</li><li><b>1 tsp</b> neutral oil</li><li><b>½</b> lemon, to serve</li></ul></section><section><h3 class="label">Prepare & cook</h3><ol class="steps"><li><span><strong>Score · 5 min.</strong> Dry squid; cut shallow lines across mantle without slicing through.</span></li><li><span><strong>Glaze · 2 min.</strong> Mix soy, mirin, sake and ginger; brush over squid.</span></li><li><span><strong>Grill · 4 min.</strong> Oil a very hot grill; cook 2 minutes per side.</span></li><li><span><strong>Lacquer · 4–6 min.</strong> Brush and turn twice more, until lightly charred. Slice and serve with lemon.</span></li></ol></section></div><footer class="links"><a class="source-link" href="https://asianinspirations.com.au/recipes/japanese-grilled-squid-ikayaki/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Recipe · Asian Inspirations</a><a class="source-link video" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pT1iG4RbK34" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch · YouTube 5:06</a></footer></article></div></section>
