+    <section class="slide recipe" data-title="Ojingeo-bokkeum" aria-labelledby="s6-title"><div class="slide-inner"><figure class="recipe-photo"><img src="assets/generated/bokkeum/generate-media-replicate_z_image_turbo-1.png" alt="Korean spicy stir-fried squid"><figcaption>Method 02 · stir-fry</figcaption></figure><article class="recipe-content"><header class="recipe-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Korea · everyday home cooking</p><h2 class="title" id="s6-title">Ojingeo-bokkeum</h2><p class="tradition">Spicy wok-fried squid and vegetables</p></div><div class="timebox"><strong>22</strong><span>14 prep · 8 cook</span></div></header><div class="recipe-body"><section><h3 class="label">Ingredients · serves 3</h3><ul class="ingredients"><li><b>450 g</b> cleaned squid</li><li><b>½</b> onion, sliced</li><li><b>1</b> carrot, sliced</li><li><b>3</b> scallions, cut</li><li><b>1</b> green chile</li><li><b>3 tbsp</b> soy sauce</li><li><b>2 tbsp</b> gochugaru</li><li><b>1 tbsp</b> gochujang</li><li><b>2 tbsp</b> rice syrup</li><li><b>5</b> garlic cloves</li><li><b>2 tsp</b> sesame oil</li></ul></section><section><h3 class="label">Prepare & cook</h3><ol class="steps"><li><span><strong>Cut · 8 min.</strong> Score mantle, then cut squid and vegetables into bite-size pieces.</span></li><li><span><strong>Mix · 4 min.</strong> Combine soy, chile flakes, paste, syrup, garlic and sesame oil.</span></li><li><span><strong>Sear · 4 min.</strong> Stir-fry vegetables in a hot oiled pan until barely tender.</span></li><li><span><strong>Flash · 3–4 min.</strong> Add squid and sauce; toss hard just until opaque and curled.</span></li></ol></section></div><footer class="links"><a class="source-link" href="https://www.maangchi.com/recipe/ojingeo-bokkeum" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Recipe · Maangchi</a><a class="source-link video" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=--SjTRJyp4w" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch · YouTube 16:16</a></footer></article></div></section>
