+    <section class="slide recipe" data-title="Salt & Pepper Squid" aria-labelledby="s7-title"><div class="slide-inner"><figure class="recipe-photo"><img src="assets/generated/saltpepper/generate-media-replicate_z_image_turbo-1.png" alt="Cantonese crispy salt and pepper squid"><figcaption>Method 03 · deep-fry</figcaption></figure><article class="recipe-content"><header class="recipe-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Cantonese Chinese · dai pai dong tradition</p><h2 class="title" id="s7-title">Salt & pepper squid</h2><p class="tradition">Crisp-coated squid with fried aromatics</p></div><div class="timebox"><strong>35</strong><span>25 prep · 10 cook</span></div></header><div class="recipe-body"><section><h3 class="label">Ingredients · serves 4</h3><ul class="ingredients"><li><b>450 g</b> squid, rings</li><li><b>80 ml</b> whole milk</li><li><b>65 g</b> plain flour</li><li><b>65 g</b> cornstarch</li><li><b>1 tsp</b> sea salt</li><li><b>¾ tsp</b> white pepper</li><li><b>750 ml</b> frying oil</li><li><b>4</b> garlic cloves</li><li><b>1</b> green chile</li><li><b>2</b> scallions</li></ul></section><section><h3 class="label">Prepare & cook</h3><ol class="steps"><li><span><strong>Soak · 20 min.</strong> Toss dry squid with milk; meanwhile combine flour, starch, salt and pepper.</span></li><li><span><strong>Coat · 3 min.</strong> Drain well and press squid into the dry mixture.</span></li><li><span><strong>Fry · 4 min.</strong> At 190°C, fry in small batches for 60–90 seconds; drain.</span></li><li><span><strong>Finish · 2 min.</strong> Fry garlic, chile and scallion briefly; toss with squid and season.</span></li></ol></section></div><footer class="links"><a class="source-link" href="https://thewoksoflife.com/salt-pepper-squid/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Recipe · The Woks of Life</a><a class="source-link video" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W3YxFNDh4Js" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch · YouTube 13:24</a></footer></article></div></section>
